────────────────────
+ do bind-this
    - receiver TypeId

` An initializer of a class's property is typed in the module's own frame, where `this` is
` the object the property belongs to.
for offset in 0 .. < frame.slots.count
    . slot = frame.slots.start + offset
    if bindings.slots[slot].kind == .slot-this
        frame.assign(slot, receiver)

────────────────────
_ unshared-weight I64

` How much of what typing records another type pass cannot take in: the facts `Facts` counts.
facts.unshared-weight()

────────────────────
_ unretirable-weight I64

facts.unretirable-weight()

────────────────────
_ do revise-application
    - index U32

` Counts a change to an application of a style rule that another pass cannot take in with the
` instance changing it: one another instance recorded. The merge takes in the instance's own as
` they end, with the state cells and the values of rules they name (`Facts.absorb-applications`).
if facts.style-applications[index].instance != instance
    facts.revised += 1

────────────────────
_ do record-given-fills

` Records each property a markup element gives the instance a value for apart from its arguments,
` at the argument after its own arguments that holds the value (`FillFact`).
. row = instances.rows[instance]
. count = row.fills.count
if count == 0
    =
. first = instances.signatures[instance].args.count - row.slots.count - row.carried - count
for offset in 0 .. < count
    . place = instances.fill-places[row.fills.start + offset]
    facts.record-fill(FillFact(instance, types.properties[place].name, no-slot, 0, first + offset))

────────────────────
_ do definer Checker?
    - enclosing InstanceId

` The checker of the instance a closure was written in, while that instance is still running.
. position = scratch.running.length
while position != 0
    position -= 1
    if scratch.running[position] == enclosing
        = scratch.runners[position] as Checker
= null

────────────────────
_ do check-instance

instances.set-state(instance, .instance-in-progress)
if !described
